To evaluate the model performance, we adopt accuracy (ACC), precision (PRE), recall (REC), and F1-score as metrics. The definitions of these metrics are as follows:ACC = \frac{\text{TP} + \text{TN}}{\text{TP} + \text{TN} + \text{FP} + \text{FN}}

REC = \frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP} + \text{FN}}

PRE = \frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP} + \text{FP}}

F1-score = \frac{2 \times \text{PRE} \times \text{REC}}{\text{PRE} + \text{REC}}Here, TP, TN, FP, and FN denote true positive, true negative, false positive, and false negative, respectively.
